ailers; the commit hooks ran and passed.\n\n**What I saw:**\n- **The drop:** for a declared OpenCode account, `session_service._ambient_base` keeps only the names in `BASE_ENVIRONMENT`. That list doesn't include `KIT_LOOP_SESSION`.\n- **Reproduced:** I built a launch environment for an OpenCode account from an ambient environment that had the marker set. At this range the marker is gone from the result. At `6a70de32a^`, before the base list existed, it is still there.\n- **Both launch paths:** retained (`compose_env`) and unretained (`launch_env`) launches build their environment through this same function. So every session the loop launches on a qualified OpenCode entry runs without the marker.\n\n**Why it matters:** two commit checks only apply when the marker is set. One refuses a loop commit without its Loop-Session trailer. The other (SR-208) refuses a loop commit that moves a status the dial holds for a human. Without the marker, both treat the session as a person and let its commits through. For the held-status check that is a fail-open at commit time. For the trailer check the failure moves to the merge slot, which parks the lane. LLR-247 and IF-194 require child sessions to inherit the marker.\n\n**Scope (PROCESS.md §6):** this is reachable through supported use. This lane itself ships OpenCode accounts, and the unattended loop sets the marker before it launches through this function. Nothing is hostile or contrived. Because it disables a commit-time check, it is convergence-class, so a SUCCESSOR ruling wasn't open. I didn't escalate either, since the fix is clear.\n\n**The fix:** keep the marker, named once from `kitlib.provenance`, among the names the declared base always keeps; it is not a credential. Then add a test that it is inherited through a qualified OpenCode launch.\n\nI changed no code, review, findings file or registry. `011-ADJUDICATE-1c45905.md.requested` is still untracked, since only the verdict file was to be committed.","ttft_ms":2428,"ty